module gunbc.plans.planning_consolidation

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

fn planning_consolidation_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**A plan is an intention:** the direction the repository should take, why, and what will be true of it when that is achieved, reasoned from first principles. How the intention is realized -- which work items, in what order, staffed by whom -- is downstream and replaceable: it may change every time the work is picked up. The planning system reads intentions and tries to realize them; it does not keep a second copy of them."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_argument::selection_precedes_convergence` (an intention is the caller-supplied goal, a realization is a selection, and achievement is assessed against an independent observation), `gunbc.design_argument::planning_has_one_home`, `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority`, `gunbc.design_argument::consumption`, `gunbc.design_argument::epistemic_humility`."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** planning is deforked. Every planning fact has one home, and it is quick and easy to see what to work on and where it lives."),
    p(text: "**Why (operator, 2026-11-11):** planning grew piece by piece -- plans, roadmap nodes, the daily workspace, dashboard work items -- so one unit of work, its state and its reasons are written in several places that drift apart, and most of it has no reader: it is stranded, and the operator does not consume it today. Deforking before doing the work removes the cost of keeping copies agreed and of finding out which copy is true."),
    p(text: "**Done when** (each is assessed against the tree unless marked as the operator's judgement):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Plans hold intentions only: no plan carries a phase list, item status or a done mark as authored text."),
      li(text: "A work item has one home, one record type; roadmap node rows and plan prose items do not both describe units of work."),
      li(text: "No scheduling machinery remains: no forecast, checkpoint-plan or alignment module, no time-period record."),
      li(text: "No fact is written to both the item event log and the fabric event log."),
      li(text: "Every module under `gunbc.plans` and the planning and realization trees has a production importer or is a declared root that a unit, timer or CLI runs."),
      li(text: "Operator's judgement: what is open and what is in flight across all plans can be seen from one projection."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. The planning system"),
    p(text: "**Intention to realization to execution to observation to assessment.**"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Intention (authored, durable):** the plan. What, why, and done-when, assessable where possible and otherwise named as the operator's judgement. A plan holds reasoning and the design evidence behind it (measurements and observations), cited by reference; it never holds the how."),
      li(text: "**Realization (derived, replaceable):** the work items that currently serve an intention, their containment and dependency edges, and how each would execute. One work-item record type; project, milestone and task are positions in its containment graph, not separate types. A work item names the intention it serves; the intention does not list its work items. Realization is a selection (`std.decision`): it can be thrown away and redrawn when staffing or the world changes, and the plan does not change."),
      li(text: "**Coordination (item events):** claimed, released, accepted (referencing the execution result and acceptance evidence), retired. Home: the item event log (today `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log`)."),
      li(text: "**Execution (fabric):** request, selection, lease or cell, run, result; fabric's own events in `gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log`. One typed binding joins a work item to a fabric work request. In progress is derived (an open item with an active execution), never written."),
      li(text: "**Observation and assessment:** the repository as it is, read independently; an intention's done-when is assessed against it (`std.goal_assessment`). An intention is achieved when its done-when holds, not when its work items are checked off."),
      li(text: "**Projection:** one workspace row per work item (its intention, the item, its item state, its active execution, its latest result, its acceptance evidence), plus each intention's assessment. The ctrl dashboard renders it now; the gunbc page may render the same rows. Summaries are derived."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**The grain rule:** the same fact at the same grain is authored once, and summaries are derived. An intention's aggregate direction and a work item's local deliverable are two grains, not a fork; a plan restating an item's status or completion is a fork."),
    p(text: "**Evidence has three homes:** design evidence supports an intention and is cited from the plan; execution evidence (logs, results, resource receipts) is fabric's; acceptance evidence is referenced by the accepted event. PR and review history is projected from GitHub, not copied."),
    h2(text: "3. Operator rulings, 2026-11-11 (session bright-ibex-807)"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Intention first:** a plan is an intention (what, why, done-when); how it is realized is downstream and may change, for example with when it is staffed. Replaces the 2026-11-10 D1 and the earlier draft of this plan in which a plan owned its work graph."),
      li(text: "**The name stays `gunbc.plans`.** D6 is moot."),
      li(text: "**Scheduling is cut completely.** No schedule type, time-period records, forecast state or synchronized today list; what to work on today is the operator's selection in the workspace. D5 is moot."),
      li(text: "**Execution is anchored on fabric dispatch** (`product.fabric`, `gunbc.compute`, `gunbc.fabric`). The ctrl session dashboard is a side path, useful to integrate but not the destination."),
      li(text: "**Display:** the operator consumes this from the ctrl repository in the meantime; the gunbc page may survive. Both render one projection; neither owns a work item."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "4. Observation, 2026-11-11 (origin/main and srv1)"),
    p(text: "`gunbc.roadmap` plus `gunbc.plans`: 158 files, about 103,000 lines. Import graph from every `module`/`import` line under dag/ and src/v2/; srv1 units and HTTP read live the same day."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Plans hold the how.** `gunbc.plan` `Plan` is `{ slug, title, body: List<MarkdownBlock>, retirement, projection }`; phases, status and done-when are prose in `body`."),
      li(text: "**Units of work have three homes:** plan prose items (no reader); `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` node rows over `RoadmapNode` (272 rows, 153 dependency edges, 6,595 lines; `TicketFields` restate why, carry state in `done`, `current_state`, `last_verified_on` and `updates`, and link to plans by file path through `carriers`, three of them dangling); and ctrl dashboard work items, the only one with a live reader."),
      li(text: "**The belt beside fabric:** `roadmap_belt_actuate` (16,521 lines; with dispatch, attempt and session modules about 35,000) already imports `gunbc.compute.work_request`, `attempt_lifecycle`, `compute_seat_ensure` and `gunbc.fabric.fabric_event_log_host`, and also keeps its own attempt state, metering, exit spool, worktree claim and session slots. On srv1 no belt tick timer exists; belt exit and credential recovery are failed; discovery and publication are dead."),
      li(text: "**The item event log also carries execution-shaped kinds:** progress, blocked, handed_back, result_returned, published, verification_failed."),
      li(text: "**Scheduling remnants** with no production importer: `roadmap_forecast` (1,104 lines), `roadmap_checkpoint_plan`, `roadmap_closing_contract_authoring`; and `roadmap_alignment`."),
      li(text: "**Eighteen roadmap and plans modules have no production importer;** some are roots run by a unit or timer (`roadmap_serve`, `roadmap_ingress`, `roadmap_belt_tick_cli`), the rest are reached only by tests."),
      li(text: "**The daily workspace page** (`roadmap_page` and its presentation, styles and components, about 13,000 lines) is served by `gunbc-roadmap.service` and answers 503: the served binary cannot decode the `retired` event kind already in the log."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "5. Current realization (replaceable)"),
    p(text: "One way to converge on section 1 from section 4, as staffed today. It may be redrawn without changing the intention."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Done (2026-11-10):** prose citations of deleted plans removed; `node_carrier_clean` and `pointer_resolves` deleted (no production consumer); `md_helpers` and `demand_restatement_follow_up` moved out of the plans tree. The 16 plan-naming typed carriers await the operator's live-or-stale ruling on those nodes."),
      li(text: "**Audit the realization and execution modules:** classify each belt, attempt, dispatch, session, roadmap and workspace module as Authority (owns a fact nothing else owns), Adapter (translates one authority into another system's request or event), Projection (read-only, with a real consumer) or Duplicate-or-orphan (delete). Bounded `git grep` and source reading per module; the output is a disposition list, not a standing gate."),
      li(text: "**Give intentions a type:** `Plan` gains typed what, why and done-when (each done condition marked assessable or the operator's judgement) in place of one markdown body; this plan is the first written that way."),
      li(text: "**Migrate one plan** (D4) to an intention, moving its how into work items in the realization home, cut over at the root."),
      li(text: "**One work-item record** in the realization home, naming the intention it serves; roadmap node fields move to it or are deleted (`carriers`, `done`, `current_state` go; `owner` becomes the claimed event; `brief` is derived)."),
      li(text: "**Bind work items to fabric requests** and remove duplicate attempt state; give every existing event kind one home, item or fabric."),
      li(text: "**Publish the projection** with each intention's assessment; ctrl consumes it."),
      li(text: "**Retire** the remaining roadmap node rows, the scheduling machinery and orphan views."),
      li(text: "**Debt (D2):** the debt ledgers (rung drops, recurring failure modes, integration concerns, dissolution conditions) become one obligation-with-trigger record; each old ledger is deleted as it empties."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. Decisions"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**D1, RULED 2026-11-10, superseded 2026-11-11** by the intention-first ruling and by cutting scheduling."),
      li(text: "**D2, RULED 2026-11-10:** the debt ledgers are consolidated as one concept."),
      li(text: "**D3, RULED 2026-11-10, not yet:** the control plane does not require a dashboard work item to name the work item it executes."),
      li(text: "**D4, open:** which plan is migrated to an intention first. Proposed: `gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence`."),
      li(text: "**D5 and D6, moot 2026-11-11.**"),
      li(text: "**D7, RULED 2026-11-11:** a plan owns an intention (what, why, done-when), not a work graph."),
      li(text: "**D8, RULED 2026-11-11:** work items belong to the realization; a work item names the intention it serves, and the intention does not list its work items."),
      li(text: "**D9, RULED 2026-11-11:** item lifecycle and fabric execution are separate authorities; in progress is derived from an active fabric execution."),
      li(text: "**D10, RULED 2026-11-11:** the workspace is a projection contract, not a particular UI."),
      li(text: "**D11, RULED 2026-11-11:** the realization and execution modules are audited as Authority, Adapter, Projection or Delete."),
      li(text: "**D12, open:** where the realization lives (the work-item record, its edges and item events): `gunbc.roadmap` renamed, or a new home, after the audit shows what execution needs."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data planning_consolidation_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "planning-consolidation",
  title: "Planning consolidation: plans are intentions; realization, execution and projection are downstream",
  body: planning_consolidation_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 1 is achieved: every done-when condition holds on the tree, or for the judgement condition the operator has accepted it, and this plan has itself been rewritten as a typed intention or deleted.") },
}
